# Which customer this build is. One of: celcomdigi, sesb, gensetiq.
#
# Unset means celcomdigi — the newest estate, and the one current work is against.
# An unknown value is a hard error at boot rather than a silent fallback, because
# the failure mode of a quiet default is showing one customer another customer's
# branding in a live meeting.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local to pin a brand for your own checkout, or use the
# scripts, which set it per run and keep the three on separate ports so you can
# have them open side by side:
#
#   npm run dev            → celcomdigi  :3100
#   npm run dev:sesb       → sesb        :3101
#   npm run dev:unbranded  → gensetiq    :3102
#
# See src/brands/types.ts for what a brand is allowed to change.
VITE_BRAND=celcomdigi
